      <local_identifier>TABLE</local_identifier>
      <offset unit="byte">68</offset>
      <records>3176166</records>
      <description>
        This table contains bolometric brightness 
        temperatures from the Diviner Lunar Radiometer
        Experiment binned at 240 m resolution derived
        from a compilation of all nadir observations
        acquired from 5-July-2009 to 15-March-2020
        with ecliptic longitude (L_s) 0 to 60 degrees and
        subsolar longitude 0 to 15 degrees. Columns are 
        distances from pole (x,y) normalized by mean radius
        1737.4 km, longitude, latitude, local time, 
        bolometric temperature. Empty bins are omitted.
        For more information, please see:
        Schorghofer and Williams (2020) 'Mapping of ice storage 
        processes on the Moon with time-dependent temperatures', 
        PSJ, 1, 54, https://doi.org/10.3847/PSJ/abb6ff.                                  
      </description>
